From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caskade <caskade@localhost>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:50:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Paint selections with the `::selection` background

Selected text (in text inputs and on the page) was always highlighted in
one fixed light blue, whatever the page's `::selection` rules said, so a
dark theme's selection was unreadable and an accent colour couldn't show.
The highlight now takes the background of the node's `::selection` style
(Stylo computes it eagerly), or its nearest ancestor's, as highlights
inherit; without a rule it keeps the default.

Test in `selection_pseudo.rs`.
